Test provider contracts without changing production crypto behavior.

Vesk denies SHA-1 OAEP. Assert denial and unchanged output, including a valid
independent ciphertext and both hybrid wrapper paths. Keep signing/key tests
and the positive OAEP assertions for providers that implement that contract.

Check the initial TLS state separately from provider-specific diagnostic text.
Allow either documented optional-engine warning; the required-engine fixture
still requires configuration failure.
Use POSIX cp -R for the zero-length-key test backup.

